# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Quorum MCP Server (Node.js)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Graphiti sidecar URL (Python — runs as Docker service)
# Inside Docker network: http://graphiti:8000
# Outside Docker (local dev without compose): http://localhost:8001
GRAPHITI_URL=http://graphiti:8000

# Graph Database (FalkorDB)
FALKORDB_URI=redis://localhost:6379

# Audit secondary store (PostgreSQL)
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DB=quorum_audit
POSTGRES_USER=quorum
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=quorum_local

# Quorum governance config
QUORUM_GROUP_ID=default            # namespace for team isolation in Graphiti
QUORUM_CONFLICT_THRESHOLD=0.85     # global semantic similarity conflict threshold (domain overrides in config)
QUORUM_AUTHORITY_THRESHOLD=0.20    # auto-supersede delta threshold
QUORUM_PORT=8000
NODE_ENV=development

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v0.3 — Redis cache layer
# Redis replaces DynamoDB quorum-configs as the config + profile cache.
# Pub/sub invalidation ensures role changes take effect immediately.
# Local dev: Redis is started automatically by docker-compose.yml (port 6380 on host).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Redis connection URL (Docker: redis://redis:6379, host: redis://localhost:6380)
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6380

# TTL for config cache entries (seconds, default: 300)
QUORUM_CONFIG_CACHE_TTL=300

# TTL for user profile cache entries (seconds, default: 300)
QUORUM_PROFILE_CACHE_TTL=300

# TTL for the platform admin config cache entry (seconds, default: 300)
QUORUM_ADMIN_CACHE_TTL=300

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v0.3 — Admin bootstrap
# GitHub username of the first platform admin.
# Seeded atomically into configs/.quorum by gateway startup when absent.
# Accepts one GitHub username or a comma-separated list of initial admins.
# LocalStack setup also uses this value and may prompt when it is blank.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

QUORUM_FIRST_ADMIN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker image pins (local dev only — optional overrides)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Pin the Graphiti MCP image pulled from GHCR.
# Default (when unset): derived from ../graphiti/quorum-graphiti sibling
#   checkout via sha-$(git -C ../graphiti/quorum-graphiti rev-parse HEAD).
# Fallback (sibling checkout absent): current prod tag below.
# Override example:
# GRAPHITI_TAG=sha-d99abda38b1181d1f56198f1565510de9564f79b

# Pin the gateway image when using docker-compose.pull.yml (GHCR pull mode).
# Default: latest tag published from the prod branch.
# Override example:
# GATEWAY_TAG=sha-ea2f792

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v0.2 — Project Config (S3-backed)
# Teams upload quorum.config.json to their S3 bucket. IAM controls
# who can write — separate from who is governed by the config.
# See quorum.config.example.json for the full config schema.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# S3 bucket containing team config (s3://${QUORUM_CONFIG_BUCKET}/${QUORUM_PROJECT_ID}/config.json)
# Local dev: bucket is created in LocalStack by scripts/init-localstack.sh
# Production: real S3 bucket managed by Crossplane (see crossplane/bucket/)
QUORUM_CONFIG_BUCKET=quorum-configs

# Team/project identifier — path within the bucket
QUORUM_PROJECT_ID=my-team

# How often to poll S3 for config changes, in seconds (0 = load once at startup, no polling)
QUORUM_CONFIG_POLL_INTERVAL=300

# LOCAL DEV ONLY — skip S3 entirely and load config from this local file path
# Never set this in production. Takes priority over S3 + LocalStack.
# QUORUM_CONFIG_PATH=./quorum.config.local.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LocalStack — AWS S3 emulation for local Docker Compose dev
# The gateway container reads from LocalStack instead of real AWS.
# These are set automatically in docker-compose.yml — no action needed.
# For running the gateway outside Docker, set these manually.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Enables the compose-managed `localstack` service (docker-compose.yml) by default.
# If you already run an external LocalStack instance on the host (e.g. for
# Crossplane/k8s tooling) and want the gateway to reuse it instead — avoiding a
# port 4566 clash — set in your own .env (not this file):
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=
#   AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://host.docker.internal:4566
COMPOSE_PROFILES=internal-localstack

# LocalStack S3 endpoint (docker-compose: http://localstack:4566, host: http://localhost:4566)
# AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4566

# LocalStack uses dummy credentials — any non-empty value works
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=test
#
# Region MUST be set explicitly — otherwise awslocal falls back to your AWS CLI
# profile default which may differ from the us-east-1 used by init-localstack.sh.
AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub OAuth — Dashboard + MCP authentication
# Register an OAuth App at github.com/settings/developers
#   Homepage URL:               http://localhost:3002
#   Authorization callback URL: http://localhost:3001/oauth/callback
#
# IMPORTANT: The callback MUST point to the gateway (:3001), not the dashboard.
# The gateway exchanges the GitHub code server-side and issues Quorum JWTs
# directly — the GitHub token never reaches the browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional override for isolated tests. Production should use the default
# GitHub REST endpoint: https://api.github.com/user.
# GITHUB_USER_API_URL=http://localhost:3003/github/user

# Must match the callback URL registered on the GitHub OAuth App.
GITHUB_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3001/oauth/callback
DASHBOARD_URL=http://localhost:3002

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v0.2 — Identity Resolution
# Identity is resolved server-side — never from tool input.
# Resolution chain: GitHub token → git email → env var → anonymous.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Layer 1: GitHub OAuth access token — verified via GET https://api.github.com/user
# (obtained via the OAuth flow, never a PAT)
# QUORUM_GITHUB_TOKEN=gho_...

# Layer 3: Explicit author override — intended for CI pipelines (set by CI infra, not the caller)
# GitHub Actions: QUORUM_AUTHOR=${{ github.actor }}
# QUORUM_AUTHOR=

# Layer 2 (git config user.email) is read automatically via subprocess — no env var needed.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Quorum Gateway (central microservice)
# Engineers only need QUORUM_GATEWAY_URL + their GitHub token.
# The gateway holds all infrastructure credentials (Postgres, S3, Graphiti).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# URL of the central Quorum Gateway (set on engineer machines / Claude Code config)
# When set, Quorum routes all DB + Graphiti calls through the gateway.
# QUORUM_GATEWAY_URL=https://quorum.company.internal

# Port for the gateway server (default: 3001)
QUORUM_GATEWAY_PORT=3001

# ES256 key pair for JWT signing — generate with openssl and store securely.
# Leave unset in dev: gateway generates an ephemeral key pair automatically.
#
#   openssl genpkey -algorithm EC -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -out private.pem
#   openssl pkey -in private.pem -pubout -out public.pem
#   export QUORUM_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=$(base64 -i private.pem)
#   export QUORUM_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=$(base64 -i public.pem)
#
# QUORUM_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=<base64-encoded PKCS8 PEM>
# QUORUM_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=<base64-encoded SPKI PEM>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM — Gateway (Node.js) + Graphiti Sidecar (Python)
# OPENAI_API_KEY and LLM_MODEL_NAME are consumed by BOTH:
#   - Gateway: /governance/* endpoints (conflict detection, enrichment, extraction)
#   - Graphiti container: knowledge graph LLM calls
# EMBEDDER_MODEL_NAME is Graphiti-only (the gateway does not embed).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# LOCAL DEV — OpenAI (recommended: proven stable with Graphiti structured output)
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
LLM_MODEL_NAME=gpt-4o-mini
EMBEDDER_MODEL_NAME=text-embedding-3-small

# PRODUCTION OPTION — AWS Bedrock (recommended for enterprise / no API keys)
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# AWS_REGION=ap-southeast-2
# LLM_MODEL_NAME=anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5
# EMBEDDER_MODEL_NAME=amazon.titan-embed-text-v2

# ALTERNATIVE — Anthropic direct (verify structured output stability with Graphiti)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# LLM_MODEL_NAME=claude-sonnet-4-5
# Note: requires a separate embedder (OpenAI or Ollama)
